# Conventions

**When you settle a new convention in a refactor, add it here in the same change.**

## Regions

- C# (handlers, services, repos, infra): `#region # {Name}` — leading `#` always
- Handlers / non-trivial methods: `#region # Execute` → `#region # Handle Result`
- Blazor `@code`: feature regions by user flow; `#region # Helpers` last — see `webapp.mdc`

## Infrastructure adapters (`Mailbox/`, `Foundry/`, …)

Each concern folder is its **own language** — consumers adapt; nothing upstream leaks in.

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `Abstractions.cs` | Port (`IMailboxService`, …) |
| `DTOs.cs` | Integration shapes + result types |
| `Helpers.cs` | Internal mechanics (regions / nested static classes OK) |
| `{Impl}.cs` | Single implementation — **owns orchestration** (connect → steps → result) |

**Public port (`Abstractions` + `DTOs` exposed to Application):**

- **Simple domain verbs** — what the adapter does in mailbox/mail terms: `ListMessagesAsync`, `TestConnectionAsync`, `SendAsync`
- **Not** technical/protocol jargon: no `Probe`, `Execute`, `Connect` on the port
- **Result types mirror methods:** `TestConnectionAsync` → `TestConnectionResult`, `ListMessagesAsync` → `ListMessagesResult`, `GetMessagesAsync` → `GetMessagesResult`, `GetAttachmentsAsync` → `GetAttachmentsResult`, `GetFolderAsync` → `GetFolderResult`, `SendAsync` → `SendMailResult`, `SaveDraftAsync` → `SaveDraftResult`; delete/move/copy/set-flags/create-folder share `CommandResult`
- **Query/command inputs use `Filters` suffix:** `ListMessagesAsync` → `ListMessagesFilters`, `GetMessagesAsync` / `DeleteMessagesAsync` → shared `MessageBatchFilters`, `MoveMessagesAsync` / `CopyMessagesAsync` → shared `MessageTransferFilters`, etc.; shared keys (`MessageKey`) live inside filters; `SendAsync` keeps `OutboundMail` as its input shape
- **No upstream concepts:** no agent tool names, no "configured", no Application persistence types

**Helpers (internal only):**

- **Mechanics, not use cases** — connect/disconnect, resolve folder, build search query, fetch/map MIME; no full port-method flows
- Technical names are fine: `ConnectImapAsync`, `ConnectSmtpAsync`, `TryImapSessionAsync`, `ListInFolderAsync`, `GetDetailsAsync`, `DeleteFromFolderAsync`, `ApplyFlagsInFolderAsync`
- `{Impl}.cs` owns connect → steps → result → disconnect for all port methods; no delegate wrappers
- MailKit/IMAP/SMTP detail stays here — not on `IMailboxService`

**Canonical example:** `src/Infrastructure/Mailbox/`

## Application ↔ Infrastructure boundaries

| Concern | Owner | Example |
|---------|-------|---------|
| Persistence / merge / draft settings | Application | `StoredMailboxSettings` in `EmailAccounts/DTOs.cs` |
| Runtime adapter input | Infrastructure | `EmailSettings` in `Mailbox/DTOs.cs` |
| Map at the port | Application helpers | `EmailSettingsMapping.ToMailRuntime()` before `IMailboxService` |
| Agent / tool names | Application `AI/` only | `get_mailbox_status` — never in Infrastructure |

Application may wrap infra with **consumer-facing names** (`GetStatusAsync` for agents calling `TestConnectionAsync` underneath).

**Canonical examples:**

| Pattern | Path |
|---------|------|
| Infra adapter | `Infrastructure/Mailbox/` |
| Application slice | `Features/Workspace/EmailAccounts/` |
| Handler | `Features/Dbo/Users/Commands/SignIn.cs` |
| Cross-slice facade | `Features/Shared/Services.cs` |

## Promotion (least scope first)

Start smallest; promote only when reuse or boundaries require it. Full table: `solution.mdc`.

Do not skip levels (e.g. handler EF, or one-off `*Mapping.cs` files when `Helpers.cs` exists).

## Constructor injection naming

| Layer | Param style | Example |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| Application handlers / repos / services | camelCase, no underscore | `userRepo`, `emailAccountRepo` |
| Application `AI/` | underscore prefix | `_agentFactory` |
| Infrastructure | camelCase or match existing file | — |

Blazor `[Inject]` uses PascalCase — not underscore. See `webapp.mdc`.

## Method signatures

- **Parameter lists on one line** — declaration and call when reasonable; do not break args onto separate lines by default
- Opening `{` or `=>` on the next line after the closing `)`

```csharp
// Prefer
public async Task<TestConnectionResult> TestConnectionAsync(EmailSettings config, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
}

// Not
public async Task<TestConnectionResult> TestConnectionAsync(
    EmailSettings config,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
}
```

Multi-line is OK only when a single line would be unreadably long (rare — e.g. many generic type parameters).

